    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f7c97a3_d0932a4d",
        "filename": "keystone/auth/controllers.py",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 544,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-06T18:09:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we/should we render receipt data ever to the end user? I am inclined to say \"no\" and simply communicate what auth methods are possibly still neded and the receipt header.\n\nsuggest never exposing the internal receipt data to the end user. This is to avoid making the receipt data a contract, it should be opaque to the end user at all times.\n\nwe should only ever expose the data that the user should need to auth.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 544,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 544,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "4106cf58ee51c5cf249bb53364f110dc2f0cdc7e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f7c97a3_46117c52",
        "filename": "keystone/auth/controllers.py",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 544,
      "author": {
        "id": 10420
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-10T03:27:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We ideally need to expose the expiry date, and definitely the required methods.\n\nI lean on the why not expose it all side since the actual amount of data there is minimal, and unlikely to ever really need to change.\n\nRight now it looks like:\nhttp://paste.openstack.org/show/725380/",
      "parentUuid": "5f7c97a3_d0932a4d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 544,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 544,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "4106cf58ee51c5cf249bb53364f110dc2f0cdc7e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f7c97a3_d0032a0b",
        "filename": "keystone/cmd/cli.py",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 416,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-06T18:09:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m of the opinion we either lock the locations together *or* we split them apart and not allow them to be the same.\n\nThis comment is not reason for any negative scoring on this patch. I\u0027m fine with this as is, but wanted to express my opinion that it should not behave in this manner.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 412,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 416,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "4106cf58ee51c5cf249bb53364f110dc2f0cdc7e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f7c97a3_e677689e",
        "filename": "keystone/cmd/cli.py",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 416,
      "author": {
        "id": 10420
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-10T03:27:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d rather we lock than split as it makes life easier for ops (less upgrade steps), but the problem is that for the VERY security conscious having them split is useful. That\u0027s why I went with both, and have locking be the default.\n\nIf we did lock them, then we\u0027d need to make a new config that isn\u0027t \u0027fernet_tokens\u0027 but rather just \u0027fernet\u0027 and deprecate the ones in \u0027fernet_tokens\u0027, with \u0027fernet_tokens\u0027 still a fallback for the next few cycles.\n\nI prefer locking as the only choice if we had to pick just one, but until told otherwise will stick with both.",
      "parentUuid": "5f7c97a3_d0032a0b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 412,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 416,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "4106cf58ee51c5cf249bb53364f110dc2f0cdc7e",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
