      "writtenOn": "2018-07-10T03:27:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "done, set to 300 (the default expiry time).\n\nAlthough I\u0027m curious how our caching works. Because if a receipt has been validated just before expiry successfully by the provider, but the auth failed, then the user has until that cached validation expires to retry since it won\u0027t actually attempt to re-validate the receipt until then and see if has expired.\n\nIf that\u0027s the case, the we probably don\u0027t even want caching, or we want it to be VERY short. Which to be fair, since a specific receipt shouldn\u0027t need validation more than maybe 2-3 times (unlike a token), caching isn\u0027t that useful here.",
      "parentUuid": "5f7c97a3_704a5624",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 4,
